# lab.conf: settings specific to THIS installation.
#
#   cp lab.conf.example lab.conf     then adapt the useful lines (remove the "#" in front).
#
# Rules:
# - File read by bash: only NAME=value lines, without spaces around the "=".
# - Never a password or a key here: secrets are in the .env files (created by ./2-secrets.sh).
# - lab.conf is never versioned (see .gitignore): each machine has its own.
# - Without lab.conf, the default values shown apply.
#
# Who reads what: docs/configuration.md.

# ─── 1. The AI machine itself ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Large disk for Docker, backups and big models.
# Default: /data. If you only have one disk, set a folder on the system disk,
# for example LAB_DATA_DIR=/srv/ai-lab (the "disk mounted" checks will flag it).
#LAB_DATA_DIR=/data

# Main language model (exact Ollama name, see `docker exec ollama ollama list`).
# Leave commented out to choose with `lab config set MODEL NAME` or let `lab` take the largest installed one.
#LAB_MODEL=qwen3:32b

# ─── 2. Access from your computer (client) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Used by `lab client` to generate the SSH configuration to copy to your PC.
# See docs/remote-access.md.

# Address of the AI machine, as your PC reaches it: local network IP, VPN IP,
# Tailscale name (e.g. aibeast.tailnet-xxxx.ts.net)… REQUIRED for `lab client`.
#LAB_HOST=192.168.1.50

# Linux account on the AI machine. Default: the user running `lab client`.
#LAB_USER=

# SSH port of the AI machine. Default: 22.
#LAB_SSH_PORT=22

# SSH private key ON YOUR PC (path as seen by the PC; ~ = your home folder). Default: ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
#LAB_SSH_KEY=~/.ssh/id_ed25519

# Local port (on your PC) of the tunnel to the remote desktop (RDP, port 3389 of the AI machine).
# 13389 rather than 3389: on Windows, 3389 may already be taken by the PC's own remote desktop.
#LAB_RDP_LOCAL_PORT=13389

# ─── 3. Agent isolation (lab isolation) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Hermes and OpenClaw have no access to the Internet, the local network or this machine.
# Exceptions: test machines Hermes may reach over SSH (lab remote), separated by spaces,
# as IP or IP:PORT (port 22 by default). Empty = no exception. See docs/agent-isolation.md.
#LAB_AGENT_SSH_ALLOW="192.168.1.60"
